@@ -69,6 +69,11 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each positional object to a string, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. It does not pretty print, wrap, crop, or apply markup, and it does not replace emoji codes, so the text is written exactly as given. Highlighting is applied by default (pass ``highlight=None`` to use the console default, or ``highlight=False`` to disable it), and a basic ``style`` can be applied to the output.
+
 
 Justify / Alignment
